# q38-27b-mxfp4-df2h4l4ames.recipe -- q38-27b-mxfp4-df2h4l4ame.recipe with DFlash2's two selector
# codebooks (sel_pred, sel_succ: 2 x [248320, 256]) at E4M3 under an f32 scale a ROW instead of bf16:
# 2 x 121 MiB -> 2 x 61.6 MiB, ~119 MiB back to the KV cache (~3.8k tokens at fp8 KV). dflash_select_q
# serves them; the architecture picks it from what the container says the codebooks are, so every
# older container keeps the bf16 op. A draft is verified, so what this can move is acceptance and
# never an emitted token -- measure it (acceptance, greedy and sampling) before it ships.
#
# `--reuse` of an l4ame container is safe ONLY because every rule below is spelled out and the
# source weights are the same checkpoint: --reuse copies a weight whose planned encoding matches the
# old container's without comparing contents.
#
# (l4ame, whose rules follow unchanged: q38-27b-mxfp4-df2h4l4am.recipe with the token embedding at E4M3
# under ONE f32 scale (embed_lookup_q): 1.18 GiB instead of 2.37, all of it given to the KV cache.)
#
# Converted with the fuse_qkv arch, so q/k/v are one projection.
#
#   rad-convert <Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b-heretic MXFP4A16 checkpoint, see q38-27b-mxfp4.recipe> --draft-model <incoai/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2> \
#       --recipe data/recipes/q38-27b-mxfp4-df2h4l4ames.recipe -o q38-27b-mxfp4-df2h4l4ames.rad
#
# The target's rules are q38-27b-mxfp4.recipe's and say why: the MXFP4 trunk is copied (no rule
# names it), the lm_head goes block fp8, and the delta net's a/b projection is widened exactly to
# the bf16 this graph reads it at. There is no MTP rule: with a DFlash2 drafter merged the graph
# declares no MTP block, so blk.64 is not a weight of this container.
#
# THE DFLASH2 DRAFTER (merged under `draft.` by --draft-model) is handled exactly as
# q38-27b-fp8-df2.recipe handles it: its linears block fp8 from the bf16 release -- it is read whole
# on every decode step, and a draft is verified, so its precision can move acceptance and never an
# emitted token -- and a 2-bit copy of the target's head for its draft rounds. The selector
# projection and convolution weights stay bf16; the two codebooks are the last rules of this file.

token_embd.weight             rtn   codes=fp8_e4m3 block=*x* scale=f32 rule=search
output.weight                 rtn   codes=u4 zero=u8 group=64 scale=bf16 rule=search
blk.*.ssm_ab.weight           cast  dtype=bf16

dflash.draft_head.weight             rtn  codes=u4 zero=u8 group=128 scale=f16
dflash.fc.weight                     rtn  codes=fp4_e2m1 group=32 scale=e8m0
dflash.blk.*.attn_q.weight           rtn  codes=fp4_e2m1 group=32 scale=e8m0
dflash.blk.*.attn_k.weight           rtn  codes=fp4_e2m1 group=32 scale=e8m0
dflash.blk.*.attn_v.weight           rtn  codes=fp4_e2m1 group=32 scale=e8m0
dflash.blk.*.attn_output.weight      rtn  codes=fp4_e2m1 group=32 scale=e8m0
dflash.blk.*.ffn_gate_up.weight      rtn  codes=fp4_e2m1 group=32 scale=e8m0
dflash.blk.*.ffn_down.weight         rtn  codes=fp4_e2m1 group=32 scale=e8m0

# THE SELECTOR CODEBOOKS: E4M3 codes, one f32 scale a row (block=1x*), read by dflash_select_q.
dflash.sel_pred                      rtn  codes=fp8_e4m3 block=1x* scale=f32
dflash.sel_succ                      rtn  codes=fp8_e4m3 block=1x* scale=f32
